      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "INVAHIR (1) looks the one to beat. Resumed in town and led but ran over late. Strips fitter and boasts an excellent second-up record. Well placed here and should go close. KING JESTER (5) finished 1.4 lengths from the winner in fourth last start over 1050m at this track, an improvement on his eighth at Eagle Farm the run before. Looks a top chance this line-up. ENTERPRISE LUCIA (4) was below her best last time, finishing seventh and beaten 6 lengths over 1050m at this track. Not far away the start prior and gets a chance to atone. Race drops right away after that. Well placed and there is no reason she cannot find winning ways. JACK BE LUCKY (2) has been racing in the bush but in open class. Has the weight relief and is worth including. UNDER THE LIMIT (7) turned in another moderate effort last start when 3 lengths from the winner in fifth over 1400m at Goondiwindi. Worth including.",
